===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|pyjamas}} {{qualifier|Australia|UK|Canada|borrowed from Hindi {{m|hi|पैजामा}} / Urdu {{m|ur|پائِجامَہ}}, using Classical Persian {{m|fa-cls|پَای}} instead of {{m|fa-cls|پَا}}}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|ur|پاجامہ|tr=pājāma}} / {{der|en|hi|पाजामा}}, from {{der|en|fa-cls|پَاجَامَه||trousers, drawers}}, from {{m|fa-cls|پَا||leg}} + {{m|fa-cls|جَامَه||garment}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Mid-Atlantic|New England|Southern US}} {{IPA|en|/pəˈd͡ʒɑ.məz/}}<ref name="dialect">[https://scholarsarchive.byu.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=7480&context=etd A Latent Class Analysis of American English Dialects]</ref>
* {{a|Canada|Midland|Northern US|Western US}} {{IPA|en|/pəˈd͡ʒæ.məz/}}<ref name="dialect"/>
* {{audio|en|en-us-pajamas.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|p|sg=pajama}}

# [[clothes|Clothes]] for wearing to bed and sleeping in, usually consisting of a loose-fitting shirt and pants/trousers.
# Loose-fitting [[trousers]] worn by both sexes in various southern Asian countries including [[India]].

====Usage notes====
''Pajamas'' is chiefly an American spelling; the rest of the English-speaking world uses {{m|en|pyjamas}}.

